         <div type="commentary" subtype="linebyline">
            <list>
               <item corresp="#div2-lb6" xml:space="preserve"><ref>5</ref> <p>According to F. Micucci, the smallest fragment of the text, on which she read the letter ν, belongs in this line.</p></item>
               <item corresp="#div4-lb13" xml:space="preserve"><ref>54</ref> <p>There were so many changes in the readings of the remaining lines of this column, that it seems better to present simply the text corrected by F. Micucci.</p></item>
               <item corresp="#div5-lb2" xml:space="preserve"><ref>63</ref> <p>According to F. Micucci fragment 3 belongs in this line.</p></item>
               <item corresp="#div10-lb2" xml:space="preserve"><ref>125a</ref> <p>According to F. Micucci fragments 2 and 3 belong in the lines 125a-c. To position fragment 3 is difficult, because only one line of ink is still visible; it might have belonged to the letter ι.</p></item>
            </list>
         </div>
